# Section break

Separate groups of cards with space and a heading first. Add a line or border only where a group needs an edge.

## Breaks on a dashboard

Start a new section for a new room or task. Inside a section, use a Heading card to start a new group. Set `heading_style: subtitle` for a smaller heading under the section heading.

```yaml
- type: heading
  heading: Upstairs
  heading_style: subtitle
```

In an Entities card, use a section row to start a labelled group, or a divider row for a plain line.

```yaml
type: entities
entities:
  - type: section
    label: Downstairs
  - entity: light.kitchen
  - entity: light.hall
  - type: divider
  - entity: light.porch
```

## Breaks in a custom card

In a maintained custom card, put space from the [spacing scale](structure-spacing.html) between groups first. Add a 1px line in `civica-border-quiet` only between rows that are hard to tell apart, such as a list of rooms.

```css
.row {
  padding: 15px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--civica-border-quiet);
}
```

## Surfaces and borders

Choose each edge from this table. Do not put a box around a card, then around each section in it, then around each row.

| Edge | civica theme variable | Width |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Card edge or divider between rows | `civica-border-quiet` | 1px |
| Edge of a control people need to find | `civica-border-interactive` | 1px or 2px |
| Text field people type in | `civica-input-border` | 2px |
| Keyboard focus | `civica-focus-background` and `civica-focus-text` | 3px |

[Web-app colours](colour-web-app.html#functional-colours) gives the light and dark values for each variable. Do not weaken a text field's border or the focus style to make a busy dashboard look quieter.

Use square corners on maintained cards, buttons, fields and dialogs. Keep the native round shapes that carry meaning, such as a switch, a radio button, a [notification badge](../components/notification-badge.html), an avatar or a gauge. Do not add glows or large shadows.
